# Jaguar E-type Series 1 3.8 fixed-head coupe, 1961-1964.
#
# The original E-type: covered headlamps, narrow grille, the long bonnet and
# the short rear deck, with the 3.8-litre six. The fixed-head coupe is modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_E-Type
#
# Dimensions 4.453 x 1.657 x 1.222 m, wheelbase 2.438 m.
#
# Shape reference: a true level side elevation of a cream 1962 3.8 FHC, plus
# front and rear three-quarters and a detail. No outside bonnet latches are
# visible on the front views, so the model is not presented as a flat-floor or
# outside-latch car.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no period UK document was sighted. Cream, Carmen Red,
# Black and British Racing Green are period Jaguar names recorded from
# American-market dealer material as context, not as UK brochure evidence.
# Weights 7, 5, 4, 4, total 20, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 240 km/h. Comfort 60/420, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 60. Classes 3,4.
# Dates July 1961 to October 1964 production, road tail staggered 1975-1977.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-e-type-s1-38.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-e-type-s1-38.dae. References:
# citycars/references/jaguar-e-type-s1-38/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: wire-wheel spokes, lamp internals and badge detail are
# simplified at sprite scale. No outside bonnet latches are modelled, as the
# photographs do not show them.


obj=citycar
